  "Ethan Jackson",
  "Sriram Rajamani"
 ],
 "summary": "A state-machine based language for modelling and checking asynchronous event-driven distributed systems: programs are collections of communicating state machines plus safety/liveness spec monitors, systematically tested by the P checker (and since 2025 proved with PVerifier). Originally from Microsoft Research (Windows USB driver stack), now developed at AWS.",
 "status": "active",
 "defined_by": [
  "reference-implementation",
  "academic-paper"
 ],
 "file_extensions": [
  ".p",
  ".pproj"
 ],
 "homepage": "https://p-org.github.io/P/",
 "influenced_by": [
  "actor-model",
  "statecharts",
  "csharp"
 ],
 "related": [
  {
   "id": "csharp",
   "relation": "compiles-to"
  },
  {
   "id": "actor-model",
   "relation": "family"
  }
 ],
 "level_notes": {
  "1": "No standard: the online P language manual and the PLDI 2013 paper define the language; the ANTLR grammar in the compiler is the precise syntax.",
  "0": "p-org/P (C#) contains the compiler, which generates C# code checked by the systematic-testing engine (originally Coyote/PSharp lineage) plus the PVerifier back end."
 },
